    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "@id": "https://ubuntu.com/security/notices/USN-9203-1",
        "name": "USN-9203-1",
        "description": "Jin Wei, Kunwei Qian, and Ping Chen discovered that libpcap did not properly validate the format of MAC addresses passed to the pcap_ether_aton() function, leading to an out-of-bounds read and write. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause applications using libpcap to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary code. This issue only affected Ubuntu 22.04 LTS and Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. (CVE-2025-11961)  It was discovered that the libpcap remote capture (rpcap) client did not properly validate packet messages received from the server. A malicious server could possibly use this issue to obtain sensitive information or cause applications using libpcap to crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-18238)  It was discovered that the libpcap remote capture daemon (rpcapd) did not free memory allocated for filter programs received from clients. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause rpcapd to consume excessive memory, leading to a denial of service. (CVE-2026-18313)  It was discovered that the libpcap BPF interpreter incorrectly handled filter programs that contained invalid instructions. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause applications using libpcap to crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-31911)  It was discovered that the libpcap BPF interpreter did not properly check the bounds of filter programs, leading to an out-of-bounds read. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause applications using libpcap to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or obtain sensitive information. (CVE-2026-31912)  It was discovered that the libpcap BPF interpreter did not check for division by zero in certain filter program instructions. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause applications using libpcap to crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-6244)  Kaixuan Li discovered that the libpcap BPF interpreter did not limit the number of backward jumps in filter programs. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue with specially crafted network packets to cause applications using libpcap to stop responding, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-6554)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2025-11961",
          "CVE-2026-6244",
          "CVE-2026-6554",
          "CVE-2026-18238",
          "CVE-2026-18313",
          "CVE-2026-31911",
          "CVE-2026-31912"
        ]
      },
